# Termal API

## Prerequisites

Set the following environment variables:

```bash
export TERMAL_API_TOKEN="your_api_key_here"
```

Generate your API key from the [/profile](<%= base_url %>/profile) page in the Termal web application.

## Available Scripts

- **`scripts/termal-api.sh`** — CLI tool for interacting with the Termal API

## Setup

1. Download the script to your skill's `scripts/` directory:

```bash
curl -o scripts/termal-api.sh "<%= base_url %>/api/skills/termal-api.sh" && chmod +x scripts/termal-api.sh
```

2. Set your API token:

```bash
export TERMAL_API_TOKEN="your_api_key_here"
```

Generate your API key from the [/profile](<%= base_url %>/profile) page.

## Usage

Run the script using relative paths from the skill directory root:

```bash
# Get today's meals
bash scripts/termal-api.sh meals

# Get meals for a specific date
bash scripts/termal-api.sh meals 2026-03-10

# Get a specific user meal by ID
bash scripts/termal-api.sh user-meal 123

# Get a specific meal by ID
bash scripts/termal-api.sh meal 456

# Get nutrition summary for last 7 days
bash scripts/termal-api.sh summary

# Get user profile
bash scripts/termal-api.sh profile

# Search for meals with 300-500 calories and 20-40g protein (nutrient search)
bash scripts/termal-api.sh search --calories-min 300 --calories-max 500 --proteins-min 20 --proteins-max 40

# Search for meals by query (semantic search - optional)
bash scripts/termal-api.sh search --query "chicken salad"

# Combine optional query with nutrient filters
bash scripts/termal-api.sh search --query "protein" --calories-min 200 --proteins-min 25

# Add a meal to today's log by meal ID
bash scripts/termal-api.sh add 123

# Add a meal to a specific date by meal ID
bash scripts/termal-api.sh add 123 2026-04-22

# Add a meal at a specific time (uses your profile timezone)
bash scripts/termal-api.sh add 123 2026-04-22 14:30

# Remove a user meal by ID
bash scripts/termal-api.sh remove 123
```

Run `bash scripts/termal-api.sh --help` for full usage information.

